 HISTORY                                                           204 1451
 -------                                                           204 1451
 This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction Physics   204 1451
 (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA. The         204 1451
 thermal scattering law data for Be-metal was developed using ab   204 1451
 initio lattice dynamics (AILD) [1, 2]. The coherent elastic       204 1451
 cross sections were calculated based on the experimental          204 1451
 lattice constants of a=2.2856 and c=3.5842 obtained from the      204 1451
 range of experimental data. Distinct (Sd) effects are included    204 1451
 in this evaluation using directional information derived from     204 1451
 the Be-metal AILD structure [2, 3]. Ten temperatures are          204 1451
 available in this library. The Full Law Analysis Scattering       204 1451
 System Hub (FLASSH) system was used to produce File 7 MT = 2, 4   204 1451
 data for Be-metal + Sd [3]. MAT=25 and ZA=125 are used for        204 1451
 Be-metal with distinct effects.                                   204 1451
